everyone has bad dreams whether they're  about unconscious memories showing up to  school in your underwear or a man in a  stripy sweater with a spiky glove and a  serious moisturizing problem nightmares  are never far from us a common  occurrence as part of the human  experience and they can happen to anyone  of course working for the scp foundation  means being faced with actual nightmares  not only in the middle of the night but  on a day-to-day basis giant unkillable  lizards with pure hatred for humanity  ancient eldritch beings with enough  cosmic power to wipe out entire  dimensions and a species of buses with  gigantic insect legs that feed on human  beings needless to say the researchers  and operatives that find themselves  employed by the scp foundation come face  to face with some pretty horrific  creatures enough to give anyone  sleepless nights this naturally begs the  question what could possibly scare the  workers of the scp foundation what could  the foundation possibly have nightmares  about well they don't really have a name  for him just a designation  scp-990 multiple members of foundation  staff have all made reports of  witnessing the same entity after all  when you deal with dangerous cognito  hazards for a living it's worth taking  every unusual occurrence seriously  instead of just relying on the old it's  just a dream excuse anyone from doctors  and research personnel to mobile task  force operatives and those working as  anomaly guarding security every person  working for the foundation is at risk of  an unwanted encounter with scp-990  the reports are all consistent they all  describe a man seemingly a human being  this figure always seems to appear  dressed in a business suit but not like  you might see a modern ceo or a wall  street stockbroker wearing instead  scp-990 sense of fashion seems to be at  least a few decades out and he seems to  favor wearing clothing more in line with  the style of the cold war era wait that  can't be it right the big bad boogeyman  that terrorizes the dreams of the scp  foundation staff is just a man in a suit  what is he an irs agent well while  scp-990 might not be all that scary to  look at when compared to other  frightening anomalies like the haunting  beaked visage of the plague doctor or  the unknowable horror that is scp-096  it's not the way he looks that's  terrifying it is the ominous warnings  that he carries with him what is  interesting is that while most dreams  are usually our brain's way of  processing our memories or real-world  experiences and anxieties  scp-990 seems to have no recorded  existence beyond what has been reported  by staff he seems to exclusively exist  within the dreams of foundation  personnel with absolutely none of these  people having witnessed or encountered  the suit wearing man in the real world  if there is somewhere out there among  the 7 billion people on planet earth a  man who resembles scp-990 then the  foundation has been unsuccessful in  tracking him down what's more is that  there has never been a single report  from outside of the foundation not one  civilian or even any member of another  group of interest that anyone else has  ever had a dream involving scp-990  for years now he's been cropping up  exclusively in the nightmares of  foundation personnel but was first  discovered a number of years ago after  several agents began to discuss the fact  that they all had experienced similar  dreams all revolving around a mysterious  man in a cold war-era business suit but  then he finally became known to the  higher-ups at the foundation after one  peculiar incident an agent had failed to  report to his assigned post at the right  time and from that moment on things  would never be the same again  after scouring the foundation facility  for this missing agent when fellow  members of personnel found him he was  fast asleep in his quarters doesn't seem  too unusual right after all working at  the scp foundation has got to be pretty  hard going with some horrendous overtime  hours so maybe the agent just needed to  catch up on some sleep by taking a quick  nap before the start of his shift then  again 18 whole hours is one hell of a  long nap that's right the man had been  unconscious for 18 hours when they found  him fellow foundation staff were unable  to awaken the sleeping agent his body  having entered some form of short-term  coma unsure if he would ever awake again  medical personnel had the agent move to  the sickbay on-site where he was placed  under surveillance and continued his  long sleep after almost two whole days  and an uninterrupted 40-hour period of  sustained sleep the agent finally awoke  he was agitated erratic clearly  something had rattled him pretty  severely the agent dashed out of his bed  in the medical bay and began frantically  running through the corridors of the  foundation facility screaming and  babbling about the impending end of the  entire world eventually medics were able  to restrain the man injecting him with  powerful sedatives to relax him long  enough for them to secure him yet  somehow the agent's bodily functions  remained in a heightened state even  after he was sedated his heart was  beating at a dangerously accelerated  rate and his blood pressure was spiking  to quite an alarming degree now we may  not be medical experts but we can  guarantee that high blood pressure and  an elevated heart rate are rarely ever  good signs then again neither is being  asleep and unable to wake for 40 solid  hours as you may have already guessed  when he finally calmed down the agent  described a dream that revolved around a  man dressed in a business suit that  seemed to match the styles of the cold  war era in other words scp-999  but you see it's not like the mysterious  man trapped the agent in this 40-hour  dream just to torture him there was no  pulling the agent through the center of  his mattress causing a volcanic eruption  of blood to splatter up to the ceiling  scp-990 didn't wrap any bed sheets  around the agent's neck or slash at him  using a glove with a blade at the end of  each finger instead all scp-990 did  during the course of the agent's dream  was deliver a message well actually it  was more of a warning than anything else  after he had awoken and calmed down from  his prior outburst the agent was being  evaluated by a foundation doctor during  this evaluation the agent was able to  describe in the most acute precise  detail imaginable a chilling sequence of  events something that was so accurate  that it could only have been true  instead of just an inconsequential dream  or a fabricated made-up story the agent  was describing exactly how the world was  going to end not a single detail was  omitted the exact times and dates the  tipping of every domino on the  geopolitical landscape that would  ultimately lead to annihilation scp-999  had appeared in the agent's dream to  describe exactly how at some point in  time a series of events would culminate  in multiple tactical nuclear warheads  being launched these deadly weapons of  mass destruction would head straight for  targets in central europe and eastern  asia seeming to imply that the missiles  were being launched by the united states  of america the resulting devastation of  the nuclear payload would wipe out  almost the entirety of the human race  exterminating around 98 of the planet's  population society would collapse on a  global scale and the world would be  rendered a barren inhospitable wasteland  ravaged by radioactive fallout every  detail of this impending apocalypse was  relayed to the agent by scp-990  including exactly who and what would  trigger the initial chain of events  destined to end in total destruction of  earth deciding to take the mysterious  suited man's message seriously the scp  foundation dispatched one of its elite  mobile task forces to eliminate that  initial threat removing the thing that  would topple the first domino while the  crisis was averted and the world saved  the agent who first reported his  encounter with scp-990 died suffering  symptoms resembling severe shock of  course just because you managed to stop  one approaching apocalypse doesn't mean  that there won't be others in fact when  you think about it that's the scariest  thing about scp-990  it's not that he appears in foundation  personnel's dreams it's that his work is  never done he always brings with him a  new warning of a new disaster on the  horizon if anything the ripples caused  by preventing one of these crises only  create another to deal with since this  initial incident now designated as event  990-07  scp-990 has made a number of similarly  ominous warnings through the nightmares  of other members of the scp foundation  any one of this business suit wearing  omen's warnings come with almost 100  certainty rate he can foresee the future  without any margin of error successfully  predicting the exact dates times and  causes of the deaths of multiple doctors  working for the foundation even the  destruction of a noted facility known as  watch station epsilon 38 was foretold by  an appearance of scp-990  of course theories about who or what  exactly this man is are common but with  no clear definite answer to speak of it  is currently up in the air if this  entity is some sort of guardian angel  helping the scp foundation protect  humanity from their own downfall and  guiding us all to safety or he could be  a visitor from an infinite number of  potential futures projecting himself  back in time to avert whatever course of  action led to the end of the world the  staff at the scp foundation are  encouraged to come forward if they ever  have a nocturnal encounter with scp-990  with one doctor even believing that the  man has a physical body somewhere out  there in the real world during one dream  with scp-990 in it a foundation doctor  was able to conduct a complete interview  with the man now we all know that it can  be pretty tricky to recall the details  of a dream after waking up but this  particular doctor claimed to have an  almost impeccable memory it is unclear  how exactly this doctor was able to  converse so clearly with scp-990 but  with so many people working for the  foundation perhaps it was only a matter  of time before the man in the suit found  one capable of lucid dreaming after  commencement of this dream interview  when asked for his name scp-990  responded with tony as if he pulled the  name from thin air when the doctor asked  if this was his real name  scp-990 claimed that a person should  have the right to be called whatever  they wish to be called before changing  his mind and asking to be called richard  instead the doctor pressed on asking the  man why he had been delivering threats  to foundation personnel through their  dreams  scp-990 seemed confused by this then the  doctor rebutted by accusing the  dreamwalker of murdering the agent the  one who had first reported his encounter  with scp-990  hearing this the entity explained that  the foundation had the wrong impression  of him claiming that he wasn't the bad  guy upon mention of a bad guy being  involved the doctor's next course of  action was naturally to ask who this  might be and then  scp-990 said something even stranger it  was the designation of another scp but  not one that the foundation had ever  encountered before there didn't even  exist any anomaly under the number that  the mysterious dream man had given there  is no scp with that designation and  there won't be for some time the doctor  argued growing ever more confused and  agitated well of course not scp 990  replied she hasn't even been born yet  much less classified by your foundation  when asked if this was another  prediction of an impending disaster yet  another threat that could end the entire  world  scp-990 simply told the doctor this is  your wake-up call since then no one is  certain who or what this future anomaly  could be whether she has since been  contained by the foundation or if that  is still yet to come the sad part about  our dreams is that they only ever really  offer us a look backwards memories and  experiences all warped in our sleeping  brains none of us can look forward  nobody knows exactly what the future  holds well none of us accept  scp-990 that is it has been a long time  since the foundation designated scp-990  if that prophesized nightmare of an scp  has been born and designated since then  what do you think she is let us know  down in the comments now go check out  scp-3017 the most dangerous person alive  and scp-1440 the old man that kills all  living things he touches for more eerie  humanoid as cps
 

